e07c99d40ff4ec.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333274/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55884eef-95e5-5e34-af7c-f78ee79a7cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-333274/selection/b78db9c02a91557c2424ecc7a73acb8b4112fbf1e90c6aa89501cb7a59e5e710" :answer-field/choices ["q-333274/selection/67a5b59663dd8172d8cc782a9e4e6d323f11a7b24d5e3079c021dc2a08164e97" "q-333274/selection/9d8878b66e35e9ddbb28437c73182f8ea692e658b5921731f47c42c962df7a35" "q-333274/selection/b78db9c02a91557c2424ecc7a73acb8b4112fbf1e90c6aa89501cb7a59e5e710" "q-333274/selection/3f436b94670b3271f524a4d327308dd662c266a944b5eda904b329bd3e7e7fa6" "q-333274/selection/5987b40f1dd2b4811b466ead9f7783958a52a6f6f30585cb770d24a8f28b2777"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333274" :question/id #uuid "c24f9a28-e384-580a-a49f-58c03f2a6551" :question/math-academy-id "q-333274" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=6$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]={e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince ${e}^{6t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-333274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "371d99ed-a060-51da-8f0f-7b38a0267bb7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333589/field-1/973217eda214ab61044559b958d4f918f020af63dc8e531fe1fa933df795146e" :answer/id #uuid "b463a777-5b7a-5859-86c6-db709fe6d3a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333589/field-1/17e03bcc69417217b3b1086f01e6ef596a2037f9f206c6cb4ba28db1dae54154" :answer/id #uuid "d9e9c641-5b84-5bd1-a69d-1df5d2af2e93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333589/field-1/a1ebd2482f5be58f7e4d544dab368c68ef21eb68b1b06c10c7f2bdd815b52cfb" :answer/id #uuid "9cac7af0-cd1e-5dc7-824e-d62a64ef03bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333589/field-1/209fa84188f39ea7282b4bcf63e5012b63b27540484e1e7aa39b053622908f34" :answer/id #uuid "4ca46fad-b8f8-5b07-9ba2-8f61592ba62a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{4t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333589/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "86aa0fe3-9b2c-5357-b81e-0cf721fd39bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-333589/field-1/209fa84188f39ea7282b4bcf63e5012b6